    "answer": {
      "short": "Six sine curves with period $2\\pi$, amplitudes $1,2,3$, and common zeros $0,\\pi,2\\pi$. Negative coefficients reflect the corresponding curves in the $x$-axis.",
      "worked": "For $y=a\\sin x$, plot $(0,0)$, $(\\frac\\pi2,a)$, $(\\pi,0)$, $(\\frac{3\\pi}2,-a)$ and $(2\\pi,0)$ for $a=1,-1,2,-2,3,-3$. Join each set smoothly on the same axes. Each curve has amplitude $|a|$ and period $2\\pi$.",
